From: Nura rc4p series <rc4p@nura.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: lc898217xc: balance runtime PM and free controls last

Two fixes to the LC898217XC VCM driver added by 0029, the OnePlus 7 Pro
main and tele focus actuators.

s_ctrl took pm_runtime_get_if_in_use() as a boolean. With runtime PM
disabled it returns -EINVAL without taking a reference, and the driver
then wrote the position and called pm_runtime_put(), underflowing the
usage count. Treat any non-positive return as "not powered": the control
keeps its value and power-up applies it, as before.

remove() freed the control handler before powering the actuator down,
and parking the lens reads the focus control. Power down first, then
free the controls and clean up the entity.

Neither changes behaviour while the camera streams; the focus value a
stream reports still comes only from userspace writes.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/lc898217xc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/lc898217xc.c
@@ -151,7 +151,12 @@
 	if (ctrl->id != V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (!pm_runtime_get_if_in_use(vcm->sd.dev))
+	/*
+	 * Only drive the lens while it is powered; power-up applies the
+	 * stored value. A negative return means runtime PM is disabled, and
+	 * no reference was taken either.
+	 */
+	if (pm_runtime_get_if_in_use(vcm->sd.dev) <= 0)
 		return 0;
 
 	ret = lc898217xc_set_position(vcm, ctrl->val);
@@ -286,13 +291,15 @@
 	struct lc898217xc_device *vcm = to_lc898217xc(sd);
 
 	v4l2_async_unregister_subdev(sd);
-	v4l2_ctrl_handler_free(&vcm->ctrls);
-	media_entity_cleanup(&sd->entity);
 
+	/* Parking the lens reads the focus control: power down first. */
 	pm_runtime_disable(&client->dev);
 	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(&client->dev))
 		lc898217xc_power_down(vcm);
 	pm_runtime_set_suspended(&client->dev);
+
+	v4l2_ctrl_handler_free(&vcm->ctrls);
+	media_entity_cleanup(&sd->entity);
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id lc898217xc_of_match[] = {
